      "every_escape_needs_opposite_signs": true,
      "why_positivity_closes_it": "EVERY solution has beta/alpha < 0, i.e. requires phi(1) and phi(sigma_0) of OPPOSITE SIGN. For q > 1 the Hecke parameter h = q - 1/q is positive, so the continuant is positive from b_1 on; hence any readout with alpha >= 0 and beta > 0 is strictly positive at every index and has NO node at all. The canonical Markov trace is such a readout (tr_M(1) = 1 > 0, tr_M(sigma_0) = z > 0), so the escape is unavailable to it. Sorry-free Lean twin (lepton_continuant_positivity.lean): QOU.Archimedean.linFunctionalK_pos / markovReadout_pos.",
